# Exclusion contract for pic-geo. Every rule below has a reason; if you add one, say why.

# The raw Census ZCTA-to-county relationship file, ~6.5 MB, fetched by crosswalk.build().
# It is public domain and it is not committed on purpose: it is re-fetchable by construction
# from a URL that is printed in the source, and committing a 6.5 MB blob to a repository whose
# entire product is a 27 KB derived file inverts the point of the repository. The derived file
# IS committed, because that one is the product.
_zcta_county.txt
*/_zcta_county.txt

# The facility extract that supplies observed city names for a rebuild. Not ours to publish:
# it is a site-level records dump, and the city half of the crosswalk is shipped derived
# rather than re-derivable here. See "Rebuilding it" in the README.
epa.json
*/epa.json

# The predecessor city list, built from unreliable facility county fields. If a copy ever
# lands in this tree it must not ship — it is the defect this repository exists to have fixed,
# and a published copy is an invitation to use it.
_pic12_cities.json

# Python build and test debris.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Credentials, always. Nothing here needs an API key, and that should stay true.
.env
